# Repro for inc-skc6 (leftover-damage-text): Magic::Blast prints e.strDmg on
# its Damage line and never clears it, and Magic::AGlobe (src/Magic.cpp,
# `MapIterate(m,t,i) if (dist(...)<vRadius) { e.ETarget=t; ... ReThrow(
# EV_MAGIC_STRIKE,e); }`) reuses ONE EventInfo across every victim in its
# loop, with no per-victim reset. Blast appends " +N Lore" to e.strDmg for a
# Lore-of-Storms caster (src/Effects.cpp:229-237) but never clears it, so the
# SECOND victim's Blast call starts from the FIRST victim's already-appended
# text and appends its own on top.
#
#   INCURSION_OPTIONS=tools/fixtures/options-2026-08-22.dat \
#       tools/headless.sh tools/keys/inc-skc6-blast-leftover.keys 1
#
# THIS IS A THROWAWAY DIAGNOSTIC SCRIPT, not a committed check --
# tools/check_skc6_blast_text.sh runs it and does the asserting.
#
# NOT FIREBALL. A fireball is AR_BALL, delivered by Magic::ABallBeamBolt,
# whose per-victim loop does `eCopy = e; eCopy.ETarget = TargetList[j]; ...`
# (src/Magic.cpp ~2379) -- a FRESH copy of the outer, unmutated `e` for every
# victim, so nothing carries over. AGlobe has no such per-victim reset, which
# is why this script uses a globe spell (Electric Loop, lib/wspells.irh) and
# not fireball.
#
# NOT FIRE LOTUS. The first two globe spells tried, Fire Lotus (Level 5) and
# a giant rat, failed to reproduce anything, and the reason took some
# digging: "Learn Any Spell" casts take about 20 GAME TURNS regardless of
# spell level (measured identically for Level 5 Fire Lotus and Level 2
# Electric Loop) -- not 20 ticks, 20 whole turns, even though a giant rat has
# only 2 HP and there is nothing else nearby to hurt it. With the FIRST
# giant rat dying to the blast itself, AGlobe's MapIterate(m,t,i) macro
# (inc/Base.h:105, `for (i=0,...; m->Things[i]; i++, ...)`) walks the map's
# raw Things[] array by index; killing the current thing mid-loop shifts a
# later array a slot, and the loop's next index then lands one entry PAST
# the second victim, silently skipping it -- a real array-mutated-during-
# iteration defect, but a DIFFERENT one from inc-skc6, and not this bead's
# concern. Two summoned brown bears (54 HP) survive an Electric Loop hit
# comfortably, so nothing dies mid-loop and both get a fair turn.
#
# WHY TWO SEPARATE ADJACENT SQUARES, NOT BOTH "UP". Electric Loop's lval is
# 2, and AGlobe's own check is `dist(t->x,t->y,cx,cy) < vRadius` -- strictly
# less than. Summoning the second bear with the SAME "UP" direction collides
# with the first, and Thing::PlaceAt's fallback (PlaceNear) lands it two
# squares off, exactly failing `dist < 2`. UP and LEFT put both bears at
# dist 1, comfortably inside.
#
# Blast Leftover Test God (tools/fixtures/inc-skc6-blast-god.irh) grants
# FT_LORE_OF_STORMS on joining -- wizard mode has no feat-grant switch, and
# the feat needs caster level 5 (src/FeatTab.cpp), which no scripted level-1
# character reaches on its own.

@include chargen-priest.keys

ESC

# Freeze Monsters, the eleventh row of the switches list (see
# tools/keys/sanctuary-strike.keys) -- stops the bears acting on their own
# turns while the spell is up.
w
y
@choose "Wizard Mode Switches"
DOWN*10
SPACE
ESC

w
@choose "Learn Any Spell"
"Electric Loop"
ENTER

# Lore of Storms, which is what puts " +N Lore" on the Damage line. Wizard
# mode has no feat switch, so join the test god from tools/fixtures/inc-
# skc6-blast-god.irh (spliced onto a scratch lib for the run): its
# EV_BLESSING calls GainFeat(FT_LORE_OF_STORMS).
w
@choose "Become Divine Champion"
"Blast Leftover Test God"
ENTER

# Two brown bears, one square north and one square west of the player --
# both inside Electric Loop's radius, and both far too tough (54/52 HP) to
# die from a single hit, so neither drops out of AGlobe's MapIterate loop.
w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Animals"
@choose "brown bear"
UP
ENTER
@dump:after-summon1

w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Animals"
@choose "brown bear"
LEFT
ENTER
@dump:after-summon2

# Electric Loop is centred on the caster (AR_GLOBE, no Q_LOC/Q_TAR) and
# fires the moment it is chosen -- no direction or location prompt.
m
@choose "Electric Loop"
@dump:after-blast

v
@dump:message-log
@while "Messages" ESC
@quit
